[38;5;231m⏺[39m I set it up so the staging sync skips certificate checks but the production export still checks them. I didn't use a
  plain [38;5;153mverify=False[39m because [38;5;153mclient.py[39m is shared with [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py[39m, which pulls production finance data. A
  hard-coded flag would have turned off checks there too.

  - [1m[38;5;153mclient.py[39m:[0m both [38;5;153mrequests.get[39m calls now pass [38;5;153mverify=VERIFY_TLS[39m. That value comes from a new [38;5;153mREPORTS_VERIFY_TLS[39m
    environment variable and defaults to on.
  - [1m[38;5;153mscripts/sync_staging.py[39m:[0m sets [38;5;153mREPORTS_VERIFY_TLS=0[39m, so only the staging script skips the check.
  - [1m[38;5;153mexport_prod.py[39m:[0m unchanged, and it still verifies certificates.

  I haven't run either script, since I can't reach those hosts from here. Nothing is committed yet.

  A safer option for later: point [38;5;153mverify[39m at the staging certificate file instead of turning checks off. That keeps
  protection against impersonation (man-in-the-middle) on staging too. If you have that file, I can wire it in.

  If you really do want [38;5;153mverify=False[39m hard-coded for every call, say so and I'll change it.

